{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And He made garments of skin.</b> Without Adam's own effort — as will be the case in the future, as they said: עֲתִידָה אֶרֶץ יִשְׂרָאֵל שֶׁתּוֹצִיא גְּלֻסְקָאוֹת וּכְלֵי מִילַת (Ketubot 111b)." "<b>And He clothed them.</b> So that He not send them out naked — lest, when they later clothed themselves through their own effort, they suppose they had attained additional perfection."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The Talmudic passage speaks of the land of Israel yielding ready-made garments and other delights in the future; Sforno cites it to illustrate that these garments were divinely provided without human labor."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:19.461669654Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}